                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 82,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we want a name or a number? Or both?\n\nWe need the chassis number to build D-Bus object paths. We will probably also need it for logging errors and other things."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 82,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "We need both,the chassis ID and chassis name (both can be extracted from chassisPath, I chose to pass chassis name)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 234,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be removed?  No doxygen, and we shouldn't have variables named 'tmp*'."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 234,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Will add doxygen and rename to objectManagerPath"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "I think this should just be ObjectManager. I don't think there is a ChassisObjectManager interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 236,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Renamed to objectManager"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 240,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "phosphor-chassis-state-manager is the primary user of this D-Bus interface. It is expecting the path `/xyz/openbmc_project/power/power_supplies/chassis{}/psus` (where {} is replaced with the chassis number).\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-state-manager/blob/master/chassis_state_manager.cpp#L100\n\nWe should probably not change this unless the owner of chassis state manager wants it to change too. It already supports multiple chassis.\n\nThe ObjectManager interface is used to obtain all the D-Bus objects from an application. The D-Bus path for the ObjectManager interface needs to be the parent/root of all the D-Bus object paths.\n\nIf you really want to have one of these ObjectManager interfaces for each chassis, the root path should probably be `/xyz/openbmc_project/power/power_supplies/chassis{}` (where {} is replaced with the chassis number).\n\nHowever, given that ObjectManager normally gives you all the D-Bus objects for an application, this ObjectManager should probably be moved to the system level (not chassis level).  Then it can keep the path `/xyz/openbmc_project/power/power_supplies` that is currently used in psu_manager.*. I think this is what other applications that use the ObjectManager interface would expect."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 240,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Corrected the comment to match chassis.cpp (objectManagerObjPath)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 244,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Should this be removed?  No doxygen, and we shouldn't have variables named 'tmp*'."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 244,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "The D-Bus path to sensors is defined here:\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/architecture/sensor-architecture.md\n\nThe individual sensors must have the path `/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/<type>/<label>`.\n\nCurrently the input voltage sensors have the path `/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/voltage/ps{}_input_voltage_rating`. So this should probably change to something like `/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/voltage/c{}_ps{}_input_voltage_rating`.\n\nThe ObjectManager interface is used to obtain all the D-Bus objects from an application. The D-Bus path for the ObjectManager interface needs to be the parent/root of all the D-Bus object paths. So this should stay at `/xyz/openbmc_project/sensors` like it is currently in psu_manager.*.\n\nGiven that all the chassis will have the same root object path, this ObjectManager interface should probably be moved to the system level. Otherwise we'd have another instance of this, with the same root D-Bus path, for each chassis. I'm not sure if it is valid to have multiple ObjectManager interfaces on the same path and in the same application."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 250,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
                        "email": "faisal@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "faisal-awada"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/new_power_supply.cpp",
                    "line": 1340,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "If the chassis is unknown, shouldn't it skip line 1344? I don't think it is valid to make an association where the chassis is empty."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-supply/new_power_supply.cpp",
                    "line": 1340,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Faisal Awada",
